BUILT in the shape of the three precedents. `draco.draketarget.ActorAspectText` (from Surface) owns the LAYOUT:
`messageReference`, then `start`, `message` and `signal` as already-rendered lines, and `present` (default true); the
`actor` head, the `messageType` line when there is a reference, each block elided when its body is empty; a present
actor with nothing in it is the one line, an absent one renders nothing and, the arguments being by-name behind
`guard(_present)`, evaluates nothing. `draco.gendrake.ActorAspectOf` (from ActorAspectText) is the MAPPING: presence
read with `fold`; `appliedName` and `reference` as DracoAspectOf writes them (own package bare, else package words,
type parameters through `parameterText (Dracon -> Text)`), an unnamed message type rendering no line; the three bodies
