DIRECT RUN of every discovered suite on compiled classes with current main, mods and test resources on the loader roots
(test classes on the Runner's runpath alone). THE FIRST DIRECT RUN FAILED TWO TESTS, 1156 / 2, one cause: ActorAspectOf.scala had been generated before
ActorAspectText's class was compiled into the overlay, and it spelled `rendered: ActorAspectText = ActorAspectText(…)`
bare where the gate's generation spells `draco.draketarget.ActorAspectText` in full (DracoGenTest's per-type gate and
ResolutionRecordTest's unscoped-equals-scoped assertion). The mechanism was isolated, not guessed: the engine's
`shadowedByHost` asks the CLASSPATH (`Class.forName`) whether an imported package already holds a simple name, so the
same definition generates the bare spelling with that class hidden and the full one with it present — confirmed both
ways with the CLI. Regenerated after the class existed, the file is the canonical one; the three other regenerated
files were identical. This is also the true cause of the Editor line recorded on 2026-11-09 as "generated
mid-update" (FactDisjointness's class did not exist at Editor's first generation). RuleAspectOf was unaffected, its
spelling being full with or without the class. OBSERVED, not changed: generation that consults compiled classes is
an engine property worth a decision of its own — sbt's gate always runs with every class compiled, so the gate is
deterministic there, but a referrer of a NEW definition must be regenerated after that definition is compiled.
Focused rerun green (DracoGenTest, ResolutionRecordTest, ActorAspectTest: 209 / 0). SECOND RUN:
